\caption(Fixed-barrier controls separate mathematical path accuracy from a very small-barrier arithmetic failure.)
\alttext(Fitted coordinates agree with exact positive roots for three fixed barrier weights. Complementarity tracks mu. The default shrinking-barrier exception and its near-boundary partial point remain in the printed evidence.)

> Conclusions and references

The equality projection supplies exact primal and dual controls. It exposes a
feasibility-only stopping counterexample and clarifies the projection-like routine
named SQP. The orthant problem supplies a complete barrier path and complementarity
control while preserving a late default-schedule failure. These generated problems
need no external dataset: their known answers make stronger implementation checks
than an unverified application optimum. General nonlinear constraints require
regularity, appropriate scaling and fuller stationarity safeguards than these
small native routines expose.

- J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), [Numerical Optimization, second edition](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5), chapters on optimality conditions, penalties, SQP and interior-point methods. The routines above implement the restricted variants explicitly described here.

> Reading the numerical evidence

`trace_optimize` calls the configured native optimizer through its stated abstract
interface. It records callback requests without inserting fitting evaluations.
Value calls can be rejected trials; gradient calls can be look-ahead points.
`optimization_comparison` explicitly re-evaluates selected points afterwards on
these pure objectives. Those diagnostic calls are excluded from fitting counts.
Callback indices are neither accepted iterations nor wall time. The plotted gap
uses the declared reference (minimum or stated lower bound) and a display floor of 1e-14; that floor does
not modify any optimizer update. Returned coordinates, checked objective and
appropriate stationarity/feasibility checks carry more information than a return
from a finite iteration budget. Native APIs do not expose a uniform stop-status flag.
The recorder retains exceptions and rejects nonfinite requested values/gradients;
this makes failures visible rather than letting an instrumented run continue on NaN.

